{
  "assessment": "The source provides a clear quantitative cluster: trapped-atom exponential decay versus lattice hold time for the 3D and 1D lattice configurations, with fitted lifetimes of 54 ms and 220 ms respectively. The reviewer figure evidence adds three labeled hold-time positions (100, 200, 300 ms) that lie within the displayed fit segments, but these are not asserted as the paper's raw sampling grid. The source supports two regimes (3D and 1D) sharing the same hold-time control and atom-number readout, with distinct fixed conditions for beam wavelength, power, detuning, and lattice depth. The exponential decay model is explicitly stated, and the fit procedure (excluding t_hold < 75 ms) is described. The case is authoring-ready: numeric control (hold time), numeric readout (atom number), quantitative mechanism (exponential decay), and explicit domains are present.",
